  "exact_normative_block": "For every assigned proof, enumerate its original logical steps (including unchanged portions) and provide checkable public working for each. A target statement or a bound established inside that same target proof is not an unassigned input. Named UNASSIGNED upstream statements may be used after checking their hypotheses; their own proofs remain unassigned. Reading and reconstruction are distinct: if any required target step is not reconstructed publicly, say so and mark Public reconstruction: PARTIAL or NOT_RECONSTRUCTED, even if Old/New reading is COMPLETE. Do not replace a derivation by saying it is unchanged.",
  "exact_added_output_fields": [
    "- Public reconstruction: COMPLETE | PARTIAL | NOT_RECONSTRUCTED",
    "- Original-step coverage: <steps and working, with omissions explicit>"
  ],
  "rough_word_target": 5000,
  "brevity_instruction": "The word target is approximate; do not sacrifice a required derivation for brevity.",
  "contract_unified_diff": "--- CONTRACT.before.md\n+++ CONTRACT.md\n@@ -66,6 +66,10 @@\n Honest PARTIAL/NOT_READ, uncertainty, failure or inconclusiveness is permitted.\n Only checkable public mathematical evidence is requested.\n \n+# Public reconstruction requirement\n+\n+For every assigned proof, enumerate its original logical steps (including unchanged portions) and provide checkable public working for each. A target statement or a bound established inside that same target proof is not an unassigned input. Named UNASSIGNED upstream statements may be used after checking their hypotheses; their own proofs remain unassigned. Reading and reconstruction are distinct: if any required target step is not reconstructed publicly, say so and mark Public reconstruction: PARTIAL or NOT_RECONSTRUCTED, even if Old/New reading is COMPLETE. Do not replace a derivation by saying it is unchanged.\n+\n # Output contract\n \n Begin with:\n@@ -79,6 +83,8 @@\n for each assigned label, in inventory order. Each must give:\n - Old reading: COMPLETE | PARTIAL | NOT_READ\n - New reading: COMPLETE | PARTIAL | NOT_READ\n+- Public reconstruction: COMPLETE | PARTIAL | NOT_RECONSTRUCTED\n+- Original-step coverage: <steps and working, with omissions explicit>\n - Argument preservation: PRESERVED | CHANGED | UNCERTAIN\n - New explanations: JUSTIFIED | CONCERN | UNCERTAIN\n - Evidence: concrete mathematical checks/working using equation labels or\n@@ -89,5 +95,7 @@\n End with '## AUDIT dispositions' and '## Findings and limits'. A partially\n read proof prohibits a claim of full assignment completion. Distinguish target\n preservation from proving all upstream analytic results or whole-book truth.\n-Keep the public report roughly 3500 words or less. Do not certify source PDFs,\n+Keep the public report roughly 5000 words. Do not certify source PDFs,\n images, Lean correspondence, rendered pages, human sign-offs or release.\n+\n+The word target is approximate; do not sacrifice a required derivation for brevity.\n",
  "contract_diff_sha256": "b2806ce48380c45d4cb7a4573e80c2582786f159e93be1fc69a1dda0049b188e",
